{\n        \"id\": \"7560448437716569374\",\n        \"caption\": \"Parents — don’t skip these 3 questions on recruiting visits 👇 1️⃣ How often are athletes transferring out? 2️⃣ How involved is admin with athletics? 3️⃣ What academic support do student-athletes get? These answers tell you more than the tour ever will. #D3Recruiting #CollegeAthletics #RecruitingTips #StudentAthlete #transparencyinrecruiting\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-12T21:21:30.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@getrecruitedwithkatie/video/7560448437716569374\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p16-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast8-p-0068-tx2/oUAED9fsz2oIfB29yzDBhIk1V7GREuFAT2VE87~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=32085dd3&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=HZXiqduEbILwfV9lLSXfbISaNDo%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 33534,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 3781,\n          \"likes\": 129,\n          \"comments\": 8,\n          \"shares\": 29,\n          \"saves\": 91\n        },\n        \"media\": {\n          \"downloadUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/0b9bf754b71696f6c42b2f0be6792a96/6aee520e/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-ve-0068c003-tx2/oUWA2fNJAtdIDlqRji4CIDrmeIIsQgLYbHH2eG/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=906&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=aTNkO2g0OWhpaGU5OTU2NkBpM3llcXM5cjw0NjMzaTczNEAvMjYwLV4wNS0xXjAuYV4xYSNyLmFhMmQ0a2phLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00088000\",\n          \"downloadWithoutWatermarkUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/95d07848ba3c8a6e5b0493139d4e3f07/6aee520e/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-ve-0068c003-tx2/o0DCHDJeHYfRLIAlQd84jNfGAIiIq2g2tr2MII/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=870&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=ZTw4NWVpNTU6aWk2Mzo4ZEBpM3llcXM5cjw0NjMzaTczNEBhYjQzMjMxXi8xMzJjXjE1YSNyLmFhMmQ0a2phLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00088000\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7698844742062214413\",\n        \"caption\": \"Parents, are you falling for any of these college recruiting myths? 👀 ❌ MYTH #1: Every recruiting process is the same. ✅ Not one family has had the exact same experience. Keep it personal and lay the groundwork that fits your athlete’s goals. ❌ MYTH #2: Recruiting starts junior year. ✅ Waiting can mean missed opportunities. Be proactive and take the initiative early in high school. ❌ MYTH #3: It’s the parents’ process. ✅ It’s the student-athlete’s process. You’re their biggest supporter, but at the end of the day, your athlete is the one who needs to drive it. 💙 Remember these three things as you guide your athlete through the college recruiting journey. 💾 Save this post for later and follow for more recruiting tips for parents!\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-20T20:09:52.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@ncsa_sports/video/7698844742062214413\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p19-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast5-p-0068-tx/oQ4qBTvBJE01Ij1ChyMtDaYfXBoAWiKAiAAjIw~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=54a0675f&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=lfLgmsOo3nNRuC25DKtHusqCknU%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 41234,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 1055,\n          \"likes\": 53,\n          \"comments\": 0,\n          \"shares\": 1,\n          \"saves\": 3\n        },\n        \"media\": {\n          \"downloadUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/50b4a04b180af174d0f75ed329e19991/6aee5216/video/tos/useast5/tos-useast5-ve-0068c004-tx/oIQQeEFFX6qA9yXyxzihBi1ERDrBqgVSKIfjgj/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=1044&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=aTs7Nzw0aTw6NWg1NjRpN0BpajZkZnQ5cjV2ZTMzZzczNEAtLjM1Li9jX2MxLTAyLzBhYSNyLjZpMmRzaV9hLS1kMS9zcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00088000\",\n          \"downloadWithoutWatermarkUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/ec768c7b1fdeb60ef434ff979a051288/6aee5216/video/tos/useast5/tos-useast5-pve-0068-tx/oEVvLHg1fAQhDquegDRqiVB6lEDSFEDBV8LII1/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=1098&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=ZDM3aWk4NjY2ZzdoaGU4PEBpajZkZnQ5cjV2ZTMzZzczNEAwYzRhYF9hXzIxLy4yMy41YSNyLjZpMmRzaV9hLS1kMS9zcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00088000\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7679457581227674911\",\n        \"caption\": \"Parents… this one might be hard to hear. 👀 One thing college coaches wish more parents understood: Let your athlete do the talking. Your support is incredibly important throughout the recruiting process—but eventually, I need to get to know the athlete. I want THEM to: 📱 Communicate with coaches ❓ Ask questions 🎓 Talk about what they want in a college 🏃 Explain their goals 🤝 Build the relationship Parents should absolutely be involved. Ask questions. Help them make decisions. Protect their best interests. But you don’t have to answer every question for them. When an athlete can communicate confidently, ask thoughtful questions and take ownership of their future, coaches notice. Because we're not just recruiting an athlete. We're recruiting a young adult who will eventually have to navigate college on their own. Parents: guide the process. Athletes: own the process. College coaches — what’s something you wish more parents understood about recruiting? 👇 #CollegeRecruiting #TrackAndField #CollegeTrack #TrackCoach #StudentAthlete\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T14:18:03.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@coach.taylor88/video/7679457581227674911\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p16-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast8-p-0068-tx2/oEWIEgP8EFAe9kHAIRDDVcrBuO6zimqSlEafBh~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=caa53e61&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=grvAKDfBTKC%2Bzw0MnHRCVoL%2FOMY%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 25600,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 1881,\n          \"likes\": 115,\n          \"comments\": 5,\n          \"shares\": 3,\n          \"saves\": 6\n        },\n        \"media\": {\n          \"downloadUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/776f6ea51b970707c250896c2ea25f12/6aee5206/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-ve-0068c004-tx2/osOSRu8hqIVIEmEm6BkFoOiEErDQeEABcAfVka/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=2750&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=NjQ1ODo8ODU7OjVoZ2g1NEBpM2hmOW05cjpoZDMzaTczNEAzMjZeYC5eXzUxNTMyYDMwYSNyL2ljMmQ0ZTZhLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e000b8000\",\n          \"downloadWithoutWatermarkUrl\": \"https://v16m.tiktokcdn-us.com/e85d43ad6c411dd8aa9c91fa4e297678/6aee5206/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-ve-0068c002-tx2/osWIESp8EFAeXkQAERzDVcrBuO6JimqS7EafBk/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=2971&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=OTVlNDg2Z2czNDZlZTtoZEBpM2hmOW05cjpoZDMzaTczNEBgYGBhX18uNjIxYF8yYTYvYSNyL2ljMmQ0ZTZhLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e000b8000\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7694108054333181198\",\n        \"caption\": \"Parents absolutely have a role in the college recruiting process. The answer isn’t for parents to completely stay out of it. You should be involved. Help your child research schools. Ask important questions. Understand the financial side. Talk through academics and location. Help them evaluate whether the opportunity actually fits. Those are major family decisions. But there also has to be a line. The player should still own their recruiting process. They should communicate with coaches. They should ask questions. They should show interest. They should ultimately be able to explain what THEY want from their college experience. Parents should be there to guide and support—not run the entire process for them. Because at the end of the day, the coach is recruiting your son or daughter—not you. 🎙️ Tower Sports Advising Podcast #TowerSportsAdvising\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T01:49:08.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@towersportsadv/video/7694108054333181198\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p16-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast5-p-0068-tx/o0jREDAF6IxifREgIQExhWQvqu9HDfcBSpWq8G~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=cc0b1412&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=30BtoxSjp5t%2Fy%2FolDjHX7ytXVxA%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 62000,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 219,\n          \"likes\": 10,\n          \"comments\": 0,\n          \"shares\": 0,\n          \"saves\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": {\n          \"downloadUrl\": \"https://v19.tiktokcdn-us.com/d401a8d4a074893cdb91bc7a4bac60ae/6aee522b/video/tos/useast5/tos-useast5-ve-0068c001-tx/oMWxDfiHEE4SIW7hIgqgFB8NQGRvAV6uWDGJjf/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=616&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=ODhoO2dlNjc1aWU4OTc5aEBpamo6Oms5cjRpZTMzZzczNEBgYC4zYmAyNi8xYjI0MGMtYSNvbmYvMmRzXzBhLS1kMS9zcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00090000\",\n          \"downloadWithoutWatermarkUrl\": \"https://v19.tiktokcdn-us.com/16f5930164a892b49371edf771a74b8a/6aee522b/video/tos/useast5/tos-useast5-pve-0068-tx/oorE3fvG9gZRDXFEQRiEAHBS9DxFIqBeqQWICj/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=665&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=Zjo4OjQ0NmdlOTg4NDU0ZUBpamo6Oms5cjRpZTMzZzczNEAuYl9gNjFhNjMxMWEuYF82YSNvbmYvMmRzXzBhLS1kMS9zcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00090000\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7688393589151354142\",\n        \"caption\": \"If you’re a parent or coach helping an athlete through the recruiting process, here’s one question I would encourage you to ask every recruiting coach: “What is my child’s role going to be on your team, and what is your actual need right now?” This question can tell you a LOT. Every college coach is building a roster. They know who they have. They know who is graduating. They know what positions they need. They know what skill sets they’re missing. So don’t just ask a coach if they like your athlete. Find out where they see your athlete fitting. Are they recruiting your player to start? To provide depth? To defend? To shoot? To rebound? To develop over time? To fill a specific need? There isn’t necessarily a right or wrong answer. But you deserve an honest answer. The goal of recruiting isn’t simply to find a school that wants your athlete. It’s to find a program where the athlete understands the opportunity, the expectations, and the role they’re being recruited to fulfill. Ask the question. Get specific. Know the role. #BasketballRecruiting #RecruitingTips #CollegeRecruiting #BasketballCoach #CollegeBasketball\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-22T16:14:15.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@coachmattsanders/video/7688393589151354142\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p19-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast8-p-0068-tx2/o8ERppIyfCH9AUDbCAf9FRAVAlEjVAXVEqsqqE~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=242eb421&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=Ep9ujO%2Bz1yXG3CsF50VTnECMXHU%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 131424,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 841,\n          \"likes\": 3,\n          \"comments\": 0,\n          \"shares\": 1,\n          \"saves\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": {\n          \"downloadUrl\": \"https://v19.tiktokcdn-us.com/f65a8203515b3509662e817a867d3d57/6aee5270/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-ve-0068c002-tx2/os1ZrrRBQi6IyAviwCHaiSNE9m38AxSKqBEVV/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=2687&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=ZzQ5ZTVlZGU6aDxoOGlnNUBpamw2b3Q5cndkZDMzaTczNEA0YTQuMi01NS8xL14tMl40YSNuYmIzMmRrYW1hLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00090000\",\n          \"downloadWithoutWatermarkUrl\": \"https://v19.tiktokcdn-us.com/137d39ef1d3f63d8190a465ed2b381da/6aee5270/video/tos/useast8/tos-useast8-pve-0068-tx2/ocqBku2fiyEqFEA0QbcqRqlDAEKEVyhrahsnIf/?a=1233&bti=NEBzNTY6QGo6OjZALnAjNDQuYCMxNDNg&&bt=3147&ft=arR-IqgwmILPD12WWPEI3wUl1ApcMeF~O5&mime_type=video_mp4&rc=MzM1MzM2NWY5OzM2OGk5ZkBpamw2b3Q5cndkZDMzaTczNEAzM181MTM0XzExNGItMjE2YSNuYmIzMmRrYW1hLS1kMTJzcw%3D%3D&vvpl=1&l=202611061617168E428D9EB566D30D7E00&btag=e00090000\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7601001850908724535\",\n        \"caption\": \"The Ideal College Recruiting Family! 🎥 Let me tell you about the ideal recruiting family. This is the family that admits they don’t know everything. They don’t guess. They don’t chase hype. They don’t pretend. They treat recruiting like a small business or an education. If you start a business, you hire an accountant. You don’t guess your taxes. You hire a landscaper to take care of your property. You don’t call a friend who mows once a week. And you wouldn’t call a friend with great teeth to fill a cavity. You go to a dentist. Recruiting is no different. The ideal family understands that someone who lives this every day can help them avoid mistakes. And it doesn’t have to be me. It can be a trusted mentor, a coach, or anyone who truly understands recruiting from the inside. They invest a few hundred dollars in guidance, not thousands chasing exposure or mass emails. That’s where I fit in. After 31 years as a college basketball coach and athletic director, mostly at the Division III level, I understand how this game works from the inside. I’ve lost athletes to Division II and low Division I programs for decades. I’ve heard plenty of no’s. I know the process. Power 4 athletes don’t need recruiting services. They need attorneys and agents for NIL. Most families need education. That’s what I provide. 👉 Start with clarity. Download the FREE College Recruiting Jumpstart Pack 37 pages • Immediate direction 👉 Ready for the next step? Take a look at the Athletic Recruiting Road Map, a step-by-step guide families can use for years. 🔗 Link in bio or visit KeithMondillo.com We are not a recruiting service. We are an educational organization that guides families through the college athletic recruiting process. Recruiting rewards prepared families. Not hopeful ones. #recruitingadvice #studentathlete #collegerecruitingtips #collegefootballrecruiting #aaubasketball #soccerrecruiting #athleteparents #transferportal #basketballrecruiting #D2Basketball #D3basketball #highschoolbasketball #NIL #ncaa\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-02-01T13:00:00.000Z\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@coachkeithrecruiting/video/7601001850908724535\",\n        \"thumbnailUrl\": \"https://p16-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast5-p-0068-tx/oEBiLL1tE3wBJOvBg8vBfBcKdtAiAAhwAtV0Ix~tplv-tiktokx-cropcenter:500:800.jpeg?biz_tag=musically_video.video_cover&dr=9638&idc=useast8&ps=13740610&refresh_token=64ac9e09&shcp=9b759fb9&shp=c1333099&t=4d5b0474&x-expires=1794002400&x-signature=s5jFlWggjmKXFn2taTbYjmnfVmI%3D\",\n        \"durationMs\": 180736,\n        \"pinned\": false,\n        \"isAd\": false,\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"views\": 431,\n          \"likes\": 9,\n          